# Chapter 4 — Andalus Architecture Deep Dive

## 4.1 Architectural Principles

Andalus is built around a small number of load-bearing principles. Understanding them explains nearly every design decision in the codebase.

| Principle | Statement | Consequence |
|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| **An Agent decides. The Kernel executes.** | Agents (ReAct, PlanAndSolve, Reflection, …) contain reasoning logic but no execution machinery. The Execution Kernel owns state, checkpoints, budgets, and lifecycle. | Agents are swappable; execution semantics (retry, checkpoints, HITL) are uniform across every agent type. |
| **Everything is a Resource.** | `Resource` is the universal interface. Agents, tools, skills, workflows, artifacts, events, and documents all implement it. | A single registry, a single ID system, a single metadata model. |
| **Protocols are projections.** | Canonical models live in `andalus-communication-api`. A2A, ANP, and local protocols are *projections* of those canonical models — never the reverse. | Zero protocol leakage into core; adding a new protocol never touches the kernel. |
| **Security is on the invocation path, not the transport.** | `SecuredAgentCommunicator` and the `ExecutionPipeline` interceptors enforce authorization regardless of which protocol delivered the request. | A2A, ANP, CLI, and in-process calls all get identical security guarantees. |
| **Durability is a first-class concern.** | Checkpoints, journaled executions, durable A2A tasks, and resumable workflows are built-in, not bolted on. | Long-running agents can survive JVM restarts and network partitions. |
| **Context is compiled, never summarized.** | The context compiler reduces *scope* (which members/files are shown), never *fidelity* (how they're shown). Every surviving character is verbatim source. | No hallucinated summaries poisoning the model's view of the codebase. |
| **Blind spots are disclosed, not hidden.** | When static analysis can't resolve a call (reflection, event annotations, name collisions), the resolver reports it as a diagnostic. | Users know exactly what the context compiler might have missed. |

