## 4.7 Knowledge Subsystem

The knowledge subsystem is domain-neutral by design. It represents *any* unit of knowledge — a legal article, a company policy, a document section, a research finding — with a uniform model that carries provenance, authority, validity, classification, sensitivity, and trust.

### 4.7.1 The Knowledge Item Model

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class KnowledgeItem {
        +String id
        +String sourceId
        +String type
        +String title
        +String content
        +Map metadata
        +KnowledgeProvenance provenance
        +KnowledgeAuthority authority
        +KnowledgeValidity validity
        +KnowledgeClassification classification
        +KnowledgeSensitivity sensitivity
        +KnowledgeTrustLevel trustLevel
        +long revision
        +isCurrentlyValid(Instant) boolean
        +isAuthoritative() boolean
    }

    class KnowledgeProvenance {
        +String sourceUri
        +String documentId
        +String locator
        +Instant observedAt
    }

    class KnowledgeAuthority {
        +String kind
        +String issuer
        +int rank
