# Chapter 5 — Sequence Diagrams

## 5.1 Agent Execution Lifecycle

The complete lifecycle from request to response, showing every durable subsystem touched.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Caller
    participant F as AgentInvocationFactory
    participant P as ExecutionPipeline
    participant T as TraceInterceptor
    participant A as AuthorizationInterceptor
    participant O as ObligationInterceptor
    participant TO as TimeoutInterceptor
    participant R as RetryInterceptor
    participant H as Terminal Handler
    participant K as Execution Kernel
    participant CK as CheckpointStore
    participant EL as EventLedger
    participant EX as ExecutionCache

    C->>F: root(request, security)
    F-->>C: AgentInvocation(execId, traceId)

    C->>P: execute(invocation)
    P->>P: transition(RUNNING)

    P->>T: intercept
    T->>T: start span(traceId)
    T->>A: proceed

    A->>A: authorize(capability, action)
    alt denied
        A-->>C: AuthorizationException
    end
    A->>O: proceed

    O->>O: execute obligations
    Note over O: audit, rate-limit,<br/>HITL if required
    O->>TO: proceed

    TO->>TO: schedule timeout
    TO->>R: proceed

    R->>R: wrap with retry policy
    R->>H: proceed

    H->>K: executeAgent(definition, request)
    K->>CK: save(executionId, context)
    K->>EL: record(EXECUTION_STARTED)

    loop ReAct loop
        K->>EX: lookup(TOOL, argsHash)
        alt cache hit
            EX-->>K: cached result
            K->>EL: record(TOOL_CACHE_HIT)
        else cache miss
            K->>K: execute tool
            K->>EX: store(entry)
            K->>EL: record(TOOL_EXECUTED)
        end
        K->>CK: save(executionId, context)
    end

    K->>EL: record(EXECUTION_COMPLETED)
    K-->>H: AgentResult
    H-->>R: result
    R-->>TO: result
    TO-->>O: result
    O->>O: execute AFTER obligations
    O-->>A: result
    A-->>T: result
    T->>T: end span
    T-->>P: result

    P->>P: transition(COMPLETED)
    P-->>C: AgentResult
```

## 5.2 ReAct Loop with Tool Execution

The core reasoning loop used by `ReActAgent`, `PlanAndSolveAgent`, `ReflectionAgent`, and `ResearchAgent`.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant A as ReActAgent
    participant M as Memory
    participant P as Provider
    participant TR as ToolRegistry
    participant TE as ToolExecutorBridge
    participant CB as CircuitBreaker
    participant T as Tool

    U->>A: send(userInput, listener)
    A->>M: addMessage(userText)

    loop Until done or budget exhausted
        A->>A: saveCheckpoint()
        A->>M: getHistory()
        M-->>A: messages

        A->>P: streamChat(history, systemPrompt, toolSpecs)
        P-->>A: StreamEvent.TextDelta
        A->>U: listener.onTextDelta

        alt tool call requested
            P-->>A: StreamEvent.ToolUseStart(id, name)
            A->>U: listener.onToolCallStart

            P-->>A: StreamEvent.ToolUseEnd(input)
            A->>TR: findByName(name)
            TR-->>A: Tool

            A->>TE: executeViaPolicy(invocation, fallback)
            TE->>CB: execute(callable)
            CB->>T: execute(invocation, context)
            T-->>CB: ToolResult
            CB-->>TE: ToolResult
            TE-->>A: ToolResult

            A->>U: listener.onToolResult
            A->>M: addMessage(toolResults)
            A->>A: saveCheckpoint()
            Note over A: recurse with tool result<br/>in history
        else message stop
            P-->>A: StreamEvent.MessageStop(reason)
            A->>U: listener.onDone(reason)
        end
    end
```

## 5.3 Durable A2A Call

A2A call that survives JVM restart via checkpoints and ledger.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W as Workflow/Agent
    participant B as A2AWorkflowBridge
    participant L as DurableA2ATaskLedger
    participant WS as RemoteAgentWaitState
    participant AD as DurableA2AAgentAdapter
    participant REM as Remote Agent

    W->>B: executeStep(wfId, remoteEndpoint, input)
    B->>L: create(wfId, remoteEndpoint, null)
    L-->>B: DurableA2ATask(taskId, PENDING)

    B->>B: lifecycle.pause(wfId)
    B->>L: update(taskId, RUNNING)
    B->>L: createWaitState(taskId, timeout)
    L-->>B: RemoteAgentWaitState

    B->>WS: await()
    Note over WS: local execution parks

    par Remote work
        AD->>REM: sendMessage(A2AMessage)
        REM-->>AD: A2ATask(RUNNING)
        Note over REM: ... remote agent works ...
        REM-->>AD: A2ATask(COMPLETED)
    end

    AD->>L: complete(taskId)
    L->>L: resolveWaitState(taskId)
    L->>WS: complete(task)

    WS-->>B: DurableA2ATask(COMPLETED)
    B->>B: lifecycle.resume(wfId)
    B-->>W: DurableA2ATask
```

## 5.4 Human-in-the-Loop Approval

When a tool requires approval, the execution parks and a human task is created.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Agent
    participant AS as ApprovalStrategy
    participant AE as AgentExecution
    participant HTR as HumanTaskRepository
    participant NS as NotificationService
    participant U as Human User
    participant EB as EventBus
    participant AR as AutoResumeListener

    A->>AS: requestApproval(agent, invocation)
    AS->>AS: check tool capabilities
    alt requires approval
        AS->>HTR: save(HumanTask)
        HTR-->>AS: taskId
        AS->>NS: sendTaskAssignedNotification(task)
        NS->>U: Email / Slack / Teams
        AS-->>A: throw ApprovalRequiredException(taskId)
        A->>AE: propagate
        AE->>AE: transition(SUSPENDED)
        AE->>AE: saveCheckpoint()
        Note over AE: execution parks
    end

    U->>HTR: approve(taskId, data, comments)
    HTR->>HTR: task.approve(userId, data, comments)
    HTR->>EB: publish(TaskApprovedEvent)
    EB->>AR: handleTaskApproved(event)
    AR->>AE: resume(threadId)
    AE->>AE: transition(RESUMING → RUNNING)
    Note over AE: execution continues
```

## 5.5 Knowledge-Governed Retrieval

The full knowledge pipeline from query to verified response.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Agent
    participant KR as KnowledgeResolver
    participant KS as KnowledgeSource(s)
    participant SEL as KnowledgeSelector
    participant FUS as EvidenceFusionEngine
    participant VF as AnswerVerificationEngine
    participant CP as VerifiedResponseCompiler
    participant PR as ProvenanceService
    participant AR as ArtifactService

    A->>KR: resolve(query, context)
