## 7.2 Building a Custom Tool

### Tool with Capabilities

```java
public class GitCommitTool implements Tool {
    @Override
    public Collection<Capability> toolCapabilities() {
        return List.of(
            new DomainScope("git"),
            Capability.requiresApproval("destructive")
        );
    }

    @Override
    public ToolDescriptor descriptor() {
        return SimpleToolDescriptor.of(
            "git-commit",
            "Creates a git commit",
            Map.of(
                "type", "object",
                "properties", Map.of(
                    "message", Map.of("type", "string")
                ),
                "required", List.of("message")
            )
        );
    }

    @Override
    public CompletableFuture<ToolResult> execute(ToolInvocation inv, ToolContext ctx) {
        String message = (String) inv.arguments().get("message");
        try {
            Process p = new ProcessBuilder("git", "commit", "-m", message).start();
            int exit = p.waitFor();
            return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(
                exit == 0
                    ? SimpleToolResult.success(Map.of("committed", true))
                    : SimpleToolResult.failure("git commit failed")
            );
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(SimpleToolResult.failure(e.getMessage()));
        }
    }

    // id(), type(), metadata() as before
}
```

