### Custom detector

```java
@ApplicationScoped
public class ProfanityDetector implements GuardrailDetectorPlugin {
    private static final Set<String> BAD_WORDS = Set.of(/* ... */);

    @Override public String id() { return "profanity-detector"; }
    @Override public String name() { return "Profanity Detector"; }
    @Override public String version() { return "1.0.0"; }
    @Override public String description() { return "Detects profanity"; }
    @Override public String getCategory() { return "profanity"; }
    @Override public DetectionSeverity getSeverity() { return DetectionSeverity.WARN; }

    @Override
    public CheckPhase[] applicablePhases() {
        return new CheckPhase[]{ CheckPhase.PRE_EXECUTION, CheckPhase.POST_EXECUTION };
    }

    @Override
    public Uni<DetectionResult> detect(String text, Map<String, Object> metadata) {
        String lower = text.toLowerCase();
        List<Finding> findings = BAD_WORDS.stream()
            .filter(lower::contains)
            .map(w -> new Finding("PROFANITY", w,
                lower.indexOf(w), lower.indexOf(w) + w.length(), 1.0))
            .toList();

        return Uni.createFrom().item(
            findings.isEmpty()
                ? DetectionResult.safe(id(), getCategory())
                : DetectionResult.warning(id(), getCategory(), "Profanity detected", findings)
        );
    }
}
```

### Wire guardrails into tool execution

The `DefaultToolGuardrailCheck` bean (provided by `andalus-guardrails-runtime`) is automatically discovered by CDI and plugged into `DefaultAgentToolExecutor`.

