## 10.5 Custom Knowledge Sources

```java
public class ConfluenceKnowledgeSource implements KnowledgeSource {
    private final ConfluenceClient confluence;

    @Override public String id() { return "confluence"; }

    @Override
    public KnowledgeSourceDescriptor descriptor() {
        return new KnowledgeSourceDescriptor(
            "confluence", "Confluence Wiki", "wiki", true,
            Map.of("baseUrl", confluence.baseUrl())
        );
    }

    @Override
    public CompletionStage<KnowledgeResult> query(
            KnowledgeQuery query, KnowledgeContext context) {
        return confluence.search(query.text(), query.topK())
            .thenApply(pages -> {
                List<KnowledgeEvidence> evidence = pages.stream()
                    .map(page -> new KnowledgeEvidence(
                        new KnowledgeItem(
                            page.id(), "confluence", "wiki-page",
                            page.title(), page.body(),
                            Map.of(),
                            KnowledgeProvenance.of(page.url()),
                            KnowledgeAuthority.informational(),
                            KnowledgeValidity.active()
                        ),
                        page.score(),
                        "confluence-search",
                        Map.of()
                    ))
                    .toList();
                return new KnowledgeResult(query, evidence, Map.of(), Instant.now());
            });
    }

    @Override
    public boolean isHealthy() {
        return confluence.ping();
    }
}
```

Register:

```java
DefaultKnowledgeRegistry registry = new DefaultKnowledgeRegistry();
registry.register(new ConfluenceKnowledgeSource(confluenceClient));
```

